Subject: [PATCH] core: use dlopen ONNX Runtime instead of build-time download

The `fastembed` dependency defaults to `ort/download-binaries`, which makes
`ort-sys` fetch a prebuilt ONNX Runtime archive over the network during the
build. Nix builds run in a sandbox with no network access, so that fetch
fails and the whole workspace fails to compile.

Switch the non-Windows `fastembed` feature set from `ort-download-binaries-*`
to `ort-load-dynamic`. `ort` then resolves libonnxruntime at runtime via
`dlopen` (path supplied through `ORT_DYLIB_PATH`), so the build needs no
network and the resulting binary links against the ONNX Runtime provided by
the Nix closure. `magika` already pins `ort` with only `ndarray, std`, so
Cargo's workspace feature unification puts `ort` into load-dynamic mode for
every consumer.

This is the minimal change required to build under Nix and does not disable
any functionality: fastembed/magika still work once `ORT_DYLIB_PATH` points
at a compatible `libonnxruntime` (wired up by the package derivation).

--- a/crates/headroom-core/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/headroom-core/Cargo.toml
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@ http = "1"
 [target.'cfg(not(windows))'.dependencies]
 fastembed = { version = "5", default-features = false, features = [
     "hf-hub-rustls-tls",
-    "ort-download-binaries-rustls-tls",
+    "ort-load-dynamic",
     "image-models",
 ] }
